From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunxiaopeng <sunxiaopeng@canaan-creative.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:27:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: canaan: k230-inno: runtime codec route, sdi1 capture,
 S24_LE

Three related gaps kept the K230 audio path from covering boards that
need more than a single fixed internal-codec stereo link.

Runtime "Codec Route" switch
-----------------------------

The machine driver hard-coded audio_i2s_enable_audio_codec(true) in
probe, so the I2S bus was permanently wired to the internal INNO codec
and an external digital I2S microphone on IO34 could never be reached.
Selecting one or the other meant editing this file and rebuilding the
kernel.

Expose the SoC's single audio MUX (PDM_CONTROL_REG_0 bit5,
audio_codec_bypass) as an ALSA enum control instead:

  amixer -c0 cset name='Codec Route' 'External I2S'

Note the bit is not capture-only: it moves capture and playback
together. With "External I2S" selected, capture comes from IO34 and
playback goes out of IO35, so an external I2S DAC is needed for
playback and the internal codec is entirely unused. Because both
directions follow the one bit, re-routing under a running stream would
corrupt them both, so the previously empty startup/shutdown ops now
refcount open substreams and return -EBUSY while any is open.
snd_soc_link_shutdown() is only called for a startup that returned 0,
so the count cannot leak on the open error path.

An optional "canaan,i2s-route" property picks the power-on default for
boards that are built with only an external microphone; it defaults to
the internal codec, so existing device trees keep their current
behaviour bit for bit. The three audio_i2s_*() calls move ahead of
devm_snd_soc_register_card() so the route is established before the
card can be opened.

Four-channel capture (sdi1)
----------------------------

The I2S controller has two receive channel pairs. sdi0 sits behind the
audio_codec_bypass MUX and is what "Codec Route" switches; sdi1 has no
MUX in front of it and can only come from IO36. Using both gives a
four-channel capture - typically the board analog microphone through
the internal codec together with an external digital I2S microphone,
sample aligned in one stream.

sdi1 was unreachable because the link had a single CODEC DAI and the
inno codec declares channels_max = 2, so snd_soc_runtime_calc_hw()
clamped capture to two channels. The controller itself is already
capable: dw_i2s_config() enables RER0..RER(chan_nr/2 - 1) as needed.

Add an optional "canaan,rx1-source" property. When it enables sdi1 the
link gets a second, dummy CODEC DAI, which makes
snd_soc_runtime_calc_hw() drop the CODEC channel limits in favour of
the CPU DAI's. Neither the codec driver nor the controller driver
needs to change; the codec still only ever sees sdi0/sdo0.

Because the CPU DAI reports whatever I2S_COMP_PARAM_1 says, which can
exceed the two sources that actually exist, k230_inno_startup() now
constrains capture to the number of channels really wired up and
playback to stereo. The constraint runs before the stream_users
reference is taken: ASoC does not call shutdown() when startup() fails.

This also makes "canaan,k230-audio-codec" optional, so a board with no
internal codec can use a dummy in its place, and moves the card, the
DAI link and its components out of file-static storage - probe() now
builds the codec list per device, and ASoC writes back into
dai_link->dai_fmt.

24/32-bit capture and playback
--------------------------------

k230_inno_codec_dai_hw_params() has handled SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE
since the driver was written - it maps it to a 24-bit I2S word length,
the same way it maps S16_LE to 16 and S32_LE to 32. The format mask
never listed S24_LE though, so ASoC intersected it away and userspace
could not select it. The I2S controller offers S24_LE (canaan-dwc-i2s.c
has an SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE case setting xfer_resolution 0x04), and
the vendor reference implementation documents the internal codec as
supporting 16- and 24-bit, so the codec was the only thing blocking it.
Add S24_LE to the mask; S16_LE and S32_LE are unaffected.

Separately, dw_i2s_hw_params() sets play_dma_data.dt.addr_width only in
the SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE branch. The S24_LE and S32_LE branches set
capture_dma_data.dt.addr_width and leave the playback side alone, and
dw_configure_dai_by_dt() never initialises it either. Since dev comes
from devm_kzalloc(), addr_width is DMA_SLAVE_BUSWIDTH_UNDEFINED after
probe, or stale 2-bytes if an S16_LE stream ran earlier, so the DMA
channel is configured with a source width that does not match the four
bytes per sample ALSA hands over: playback at 24/32 bits is silent.
Mirror the capture side's DMA_SLAVE_BUSWIDTH_4_BYTES onto playback.

Existing device trees are unaffected: both new properties default to
the previous behaviour, so a link with one real codec, two channels,
and no format/DMA change for S16_LE.

Signed-off-by: Sun Xiaopeng <sunxiaopeng@canaan-creative.com>
